      "writtenOn": "2023-11-10T12:11:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will break once we extend the topology to multiple devices per pvIOMMU.\n\nWhat about treating pvIOMMUs as another special set of assigned devices by introducing `DeviceAssignmentInfo::(assigned_)pviommus: BTreeSet\u003cu32\u003e` of `id`? You\u0027d get the uniqueness check in the ctor for free and could implement `patch` like this:\n\nFirst, patch the template pvIOMMUs, recording their DTC-generated phandles [*]:\n\n```\nlet mut compatible \u003d fdt.root_mut()?.next_compatible(PVIOMMU_COMPATIBLE)?;\nlet mut pviommu_phandles: BTreeMap\u003cu32, Phandle\u003e;\nfor id in self.assigned_pviommus {\n    let mut pviommu \u003d compatible.ok_or(DeviceAssignmentError::TooManyPvIommu)?;\n    let phandle \u003d pviommu.as_node().phandle()?.unwrap();\n    pviommu.setprop_inplace(cstr!(\"id\"), \u0026u32::to_be_bytes(iommu.id))?;\n    pviommu_phandles.insert(id, phandle);\n    compatible \u003d pviommu.next_compatible(PVIOMMU_COMPATIBLE)?;\n}\n```\n\nThen, filter out the remaining template pvIOMMUs:\n```\nwhile let Some(compatible) \u003d compatible.delete_and_next_compatible(PVIOMMU_COMPATIBLE)? {\n    // Having an empty loop body is weird!\n    // I wonder if there\u0027s a better way to express this?\n}\n```\n\nFinally, patch the VM DTBO devices by looking up pvIOMMU phandles by `id`:\n```\nfor device in \u0026self.assigned_devices {\n    device.patch(fdt, \u0026pviommu_phandles)?;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n[*]: As a nit, I think the iterator-like reference could be DRY-ed with\n```\nlet mut compatible \u003d fdt.root_mut()?;\n// ...\nfor id in self.assigned_pviommus {\n    let mut pviommu \u003d compatible.next_compatible(PVIOMMU_COMPATIBLE)?\n                                .ok_or(DeviceAssignmentError::TooManyPvIommu)?;\n    // ...\n    // nothing to do at end of loop!\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 369,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 376,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "2f6f45d85371249a3eb3a72e1144f9467061e40b",
