      "message": "\u003e This will break once we extend the topology to multiple devices per pvIOMMU.\n\nI\u0027m sorry but could you elaborate details when would my code break? I can accept your suggestion anyway, but I want to understand to prevent potential issue after I accept your suggestion.\n\n\n-----\n\n\u003e filter remaining pvIOMMUs ..\n\nThank you for reminding me of `delete_and_next_compatible()`.\n\nBut the variable wouldn\u0027t be empty because \n\ni.e. `while let Some(compatible) \u003d compatible.delete_and_next_compatible(PVIOMMU_COMPATIBLE)` gives compilation error because `compatible` isn\u0027t updated.\n\n-----\n\u003e I think the iterator-like reference could be DRY-ed with\n\nAccepted your naming. `next_compatible()` consumes self, so `compatible` needs update. I couldn\u0027t find a good way to remove end of loop treatment.",
